  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Single-phase fcc FeCoNi or a closely related FeCoNi-based alloy has high saturation magnetization and coercivity below 100 Oe.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Introducing a few atomic percent Ga is the proposed alloying intervention.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ga addition promotes a partial transformation of the fcc phase into a BCC phase.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Ga-modified alloy will contain nanoscale BCC precipitates dispersed in an fcc matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7512446::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "HEAs can form mixed BCC and FCC structures.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7512446::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The BCC precipitates create heterophase boundaries in the fcc matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed BCC secondary phase has higher magnetocrystalline anisotropy than the fcc matrix.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "BCC precipitates and heterophase boundaries provide additional domain-wall-pinning sites.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increased magnetocrystalline anisotropy and domain-wall pinning increase coercivity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A dominant fcc matrix will largely retain the alloy's high saturation magnetization after Ga addition.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ga modification is predicted to raise coercivity above 100 Oe.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ga content below 5 at% is low enough to preserve a predominantly fcc matrix.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Excessive Ga may cause complete phase transformation or degradation of saturation magnetization.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The relevant magnetic measurements are conducted near room temperature after arc melting and homogenization.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "X-ray diffraction can test for the emergence of a BCC phase, while VSM hysteresis loops can determine coercivity and saturation magnetization.",
